<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hortus Eystettensis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1613</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hortus Eystettensis is a celebrated botanical book published in 1613, recording the plants of the garden laid out by Prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-conrad-von-gemmingen">Johann Conrad von Gemmingen</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willibaldsburg">Willibaldsburg</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eichstatt">Eichstätt</a>. Compiled by the apothecary Basilius Besler, it has 367 copperplate engravings of more than 1,000 plants and is one of the masterpieces of botanical illustration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hortus-eystettensis.jpg" alt="Hortus Eystettensis" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basilius Besler / Wolfgang Kilian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hortus_Eystettensis,_1613_(KU_2894-1_003)_-title.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
